.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MK.CROSSTEST.MK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk.crosstest.mk
.Nd where the tests run
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Decides where
.Cm test
runs.
Tests run locally unless the target is foreign to the build host.
A foreign target needs a runner;
.Cm test
stops before building if it has none, rather than run target programs on the
wrong machine.
.Pp
Not included directly by a makefile.
.Ss Variables
.Bl -tag -width "TEST_RUNNER.os-arch"
.It Va TEST_RUNNER. Ns Ar os Ns - Ns Ar arch
The runner for that target.
.It Va TEST_RUNNER
The runner for any other.
.El
.Pp
A runner is one of:
.Bl -tag -width "ssh:[user@]host[:port]" -offset indent -compact
.It Cm ssh: Ns Oo Ar user Ns @ Oc Ns Ar host Ns Op : Ns Ar port
.It Cm docker: Ns Ar image Ns Op @ Ns Ar platform
.It Cm cmd: Ns Ar program
.It Cm local
run here anyway, for example through an emulator
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "QEMU_LD_PREFIX"
.It Ev BMK_SSH_OPTS
Extra options for
.Xr ssh 1 .
.It Ev QEMU_LD_PREFIX
For a foreign Linux target with
.Cm local ,
set to
.Ev BMK_LINUX_SYSROOT
unless already set, so the emulator finds the target's loader.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl $ bmake test TARGET=linux TARGET_ARCH=amd64 TEST_RUNNER=docker:debian:13@linux/amd64
.Dl $ bmake test TARGET=freebsd TEST_RUNNER=ssh:ci@bsd-box
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bmake-it 7 ,
.Xr mk.test.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.tst.mk 5 ,
.Xr ssh 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Sylvain Souche
